{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-815", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/815", "wordCount": 2421, "segments": [{"start": 22.0, "text": "I have a hunch that most of"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "you probably found yourself in"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "this situation before."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "A long list of names, a lot of"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "scrolling, many doubts, until"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "you have to embrace the fact"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "that you don't know what you're"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "doing, so you just wing it."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "But is there a better way to"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "pick fonts?"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "Yes, there is."}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "You're probably familiar with a"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "San Francisco font, the system"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "font."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "It's minimal, functional, and it"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "provides great visual continuity"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "between the system and your app."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "But sometimes, you need"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "something different."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "Perhaps you want your app to"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "exude sophistication?"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "Or feel literary?"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "Be awkward?"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "Or just loud and upfront?"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "How do you figure out which type"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "facing style is the right one"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "for your app?"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "Well, you need to answer at"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "least two questions."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "What is my intended use?"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "And this will touch on the"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "functional aspects, \"What"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "impression do I want to make?\""}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "This requires to look into how"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "style affects the visual mood of"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "an app."}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "Once these questions have"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "answers, you can stop thinking"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "about the pairing of fonts."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "But first, I'd like to introduce"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "two terms in the context of"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "typography: Structure and"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "contrast."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "To better understand typography,"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "it is usually helpful to look"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "into calligraphy."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "Calligraphy is the art of"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "writing, and to write, you need"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "a tool."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "For instance, here are three"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "commonly used tools around the"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "world."}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "On the left, we have the brush,"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "which is essential to most East"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "Asian calligraphy and"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "typography."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "In the middle, we have the"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Rodney pen or Kalamos."}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "It has defined Roman letter"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "forms, the Arabic Naskh style,"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "or many index scripts."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "And on the right, we have the"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "pointed pen, the tool that gives"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "precise control of a stroke"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "modulation, a feature that"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "really shines with some Cyrillic"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "glyphs, for instance."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "But whatever the effect a"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "calligraphic tool has, it can"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "always be described in terms of"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "structure and contrast."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "And here's structure."}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "You can think of it as the path"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "a tool follows to achieve a"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "particular shape."}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "Those of us who like to be"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "fancy, also use the Latin word"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "ductus to refer to structure."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "Now, to demonstrate contrast,"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "let me use a personal favorite"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "among the tools I just showed,"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "the pointed pen."}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "If I drag it across the screen,"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "I get a very simple line."}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "Now, if I do the same but this"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "time, pressing as I drag it, I"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "introduce weight."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "And this modulation of the"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "stroke is what we call"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "\"contrast.\""}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "So, let's now apply this to"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "letter forms."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "Here are two structures for"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "lowercase N, or two ducti for"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "fancy people."}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "The one on the left, can be"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "traced with a single stroke."}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "This kind of structure is called"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "cursive, and is inherently"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "dynamic."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "The one on the right, requires"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "several constructed pen strokes,"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "and therefore feels more static."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "These monolinear designs have no"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "contrast right now."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "So, let me add some."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "As we add weight to the vertical"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "strokes, the difference between"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "thick and thin increases, until"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "we reach high contrast."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "If I now add weight to the thin"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "strokes, we move toward low"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "contrast."}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "Now the main difference with our"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "starting point is mostly weight."}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "So, you may be thinking now,"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "\"Well, this is all fine and"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "dandy, but why do I need to care"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "about this?\""}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "So, let's have a look at those"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "two sentences."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "At this particular size, the"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "bottom line is much easier to"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "read than the top line."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "And we can easily understand why"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "if we look closer at each"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "design."}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "On top, we have Big Caslon."}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "And below, Adobe Caslon prompt."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "Both designs are revivals of the"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "work of British type founder"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "William Caslon, but one is"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "designed for this play, and the"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "other one for text."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "Now what does this mean, exactly?"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "The thin strokes in Big Caslon,"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "produce high contrast, which is"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "an appealing graphical feature."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "It looks sharp."}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "But if you scale it down, the"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "thin strokes will eventually"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "disappear and will make reading"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "quite unpleasant, if not"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "impossible."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "On the other hand, Adobe Caslon"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "Pro has lower contrast and can"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "be used as smaller point sizes,"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "because of its sturdier design."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "And now the key difference"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "between those two designs is"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "spacing."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "For optical reasons, reading"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "stays comfortable if the space"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "between letters increases as the"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "point size decreases."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Adobe Caslon Pro has looser"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "spacing and this contributes to"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "a nicer reading experience at"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "smaller size."}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "Display and text are really just"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "loose terms describing usage."}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "This play type is meant to draw"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "attention."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "So, you typically use it at"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "bigger point sizes, which in"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "turn allows you to use styles"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "with more high -- with higher"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "contrast and more elaborate"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "Text type is about making the"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "reading experience comfortable."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "When picking a text font, you'll"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "want to make sure the contrast"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "of the type face is such that it"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "will scale down nicely."}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "The spacing should also feel"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "comfortable at small size."}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "And in general, try avoiding"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "extremes of weight or style."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "A good reading experience is"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "usually the one you don't notice."}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "For display, you have more"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "freedom."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "This is the right place to use"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "the more extreme weights or"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "decorative styles."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "Even in display though, stay"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "aware of spacing."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "A headline usually looks better"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "if it's tightly spaced."}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "Alright, now let's talk about"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "what everyone is really"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "interested in, style."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "Becoming better at selecting"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "fonts as with most things,"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "requires practice."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "There's a lot of stuff to learn"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "and it's perfectly normal to"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "feel overwhelmed at first."}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "But there's really only one way"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "forward."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "You need to learn how style"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "produces an impression."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "Remember that app I called"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "sophisticated in my intro?"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "Well, I picked that term but"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "it's by no means a universal"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "qualification."}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "What style conveys is strongly"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "tied to subjectivity, and will"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "vary from one person to another."}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "There is one thing you can learn"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "about though, and that is what"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "people come to associate with a"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "given style."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "In other words, their"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "expectations."}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "So, let's look at the type face"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "used for the name of the app,"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "Cochin."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "The style itself is called"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "transitional old style."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Most of you probably never heard"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "of it, but you've likely been"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "exposed to it in books and/or"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "magazines."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "Cochin has very small, lowercase"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "letters compared to the upper"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "case. This gives a classic appearance,"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "which will feel elegant to a lot"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "of people."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "But these proportions also"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "happen to be exaggerated, and"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "that makes it feel a bit"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "whimsical."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "The companion to Cochin, Snell"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "Roundhand, is a design mimicking"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "calligraphy."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "And you don't have to be a"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "calligrapher to get a sense of"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "how much skill this calligraphic"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "style demands."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "It's elaborate structure and"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "high contrast, lends some"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "preciousness to this design."}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "So, if I round them up, I have"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "elegant, whimsical, elaborate,"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "and precious."}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "How's that for sophistication?"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "So, why now would this feel"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "literary?"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "The two typefaces we're looking"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "at right now, although there is"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "a display, and a textile, both"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "have typical features of a"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "classical book face."}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "That's why we feel inclined to"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "look at this choice as literary."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "But that kind of association is"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "not natural at all."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "It just comes from the fact that"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "most of us have been exposed to"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "those styles in books."}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "To complete this brief study in"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "style, I'd like to look at the"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "fame and crazed geometric"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "sans-serif."}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "This is a great example of how"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "the feel of a typographic style"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "comes both from form and usage."}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "The first appeal of that style"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "is probably -- it's very simple,"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "geometry, and I'll venture into"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "saying that we've seen renewed"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "interest recently in that style"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "because of our current design"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "infatuation with simplicity."}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "But because this style is all"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "over the place right now, you"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "may be inclined to think that it"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "feels very contemporary and"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "fresh."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "But the nerd in me disagrees."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "This style is almost 100 years"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "old. And don't get me wrong, I love"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "old stuff, but I just won't call"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "it fresh."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "But that's the beauty of style."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "It has many layers, and new"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "layers of meaning get added"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "constantly."}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "To become better at picking font"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "styles, you need to become aware"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "of those layers, old and new."}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "So, with our growing knowledge"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "of typographic style, let's look"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "at a few strategies to pair"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "fonts."}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "Note the use of the verb \"pair\""}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "There is no rule against using"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "more than two typefaces, but"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "trust me, you're better off"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "starting small."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "You can always add style later"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "on if you really need them."}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "The first point I'd like to make"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "here, is about the impact of"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "proportions when pairing fonts."}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "Let's imagine for a moment, you"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "have to design an app for WWSC,"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "the Worldwide Sign Painters"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "Conference."}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "You start off nice and easy with"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "this system font, but we're"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "missing that sign paintery-vibe."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "So, we go back to the font menu"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "and I kid you not, there's a"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "sign painter typeface in there."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "Sounds like a perfect match,"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "right?"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "Well, I should mention that us"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "type nerds have a term for that"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "situation."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "When someone picks a typeface by"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "its name, we call that an LTypI,"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "or Lack of Typographic"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "Imagination."}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "There's nothing wrong with it,"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "but picking feature out just"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "because your app is about the"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "future might be too much of a"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "shortcut."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "So, if you're going to pick it,"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "make sure it's because the style"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "is appropriate and it serves its"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "functional purpose."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "At the end of the day, a"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "should really just"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "be the cherry on top of the"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "cake."}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "So, back to this cherry, I'll"}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "risk offending a few of my"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "peers."}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "You start working on a schedule"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "for the event, and you decide to"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "use both fonts for typographic"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "contrast, SF and sign painter."}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "But something's off."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "The title's look smaller."}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "And to make them look matched,"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "we'll have to increase the point"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "size on that sign painter style."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Now, where does this difference"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "come from?"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "Type designers draw glyphs"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "within the bounds of a virtual"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "box called a font body."}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "Inside this box, proportion will"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "vary from one design to another."}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "The height of a font's body is"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "what is referred to as the point"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "size."}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "So, at the same point size, two"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "fonts can appear to have"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "different scales because of"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "their design."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "Let me show you how this could"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "be relevant."}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "Let's say you're working on a"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "dictionary app."}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "Dictionaries require a lot of"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "typographic hierarchy, and using"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "only the weights and italics of"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "a might not be enough."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "You have those descriptives"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "stand out, for instance."}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "So, we decide to go look for a"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "serif typeface to create"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "typographic contrast."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "And to try and avoid to tweak"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "point sizes left and right,"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "let's find a serif typeface that"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "has close proportions to the"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "This is easily done by setting"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "all candidates side by side."}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "They're the same point size and"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "evaluating their apparent scale."}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "There is nothing wrong with"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "picking a typeface of smaller or"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "greater scale, but just bear in"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "mind that you'll have to adjust"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "point size if you go with that"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "twice."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "So, let's make our life easier"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "here and look for the closest"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "match available."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "And we have a winner."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "Now, bringing that back in our"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "layout, we introduce typographic"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "contrast, and we're done."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "No need to tweak point sizes."}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "If you're worried that this approach might limit your"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "stylistic options, please don't."}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "There are thousands of good"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "typefaces out there, and quite a"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "few type designers release from"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "families, with multiple styles"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "of consistent proportions."}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "So, let's now experiment a bit"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "with pairing text and display"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "styles."}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "So, let's start nice and easy"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "again with a in a"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "news story layout."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "This typographic layout has"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "strong stylistic continuity."}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "The only difference between text"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "and headline, are size and the"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "use of italics."}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "But we might be after something"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "with a bit more of a punch."}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "And the first way to get there,"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "the easiest way to get there, is"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "to first leverage weight."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "Sticking to a single typeface"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "and pairing some of its variant,"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "is a very efficient way to"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "achieve design consistency."}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "But since we're here to"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "experiment, let's keep on trying"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "things."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "We now change the kind of"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "typographic contrast from a"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "weight difference to a stylistic"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "difference."}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "When doing these kind of"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "pairings, make sure that the"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "stylistic difference is strong"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "enough to be obvious."}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "Here we have two typestyles of"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "both different structures, and"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "stroke contrast, so we're in a"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "good place."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "By the way, it is sometimes good"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "enough to have a strong display"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "typeface and using the system"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "font at the same time."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "You're defining your own style,"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "but also taking advantage of"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "performance as a"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "typographic workhorse."}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "But let's keep on experimenting"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "anyway."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "I think I'd like to use a serif"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "typeface down there."}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "We return to an understated and"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "calm effect like we had in the"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "beginning, but with a quite"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "different flavor."}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "This will now feel more bookish"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "because of the type choice, but"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "also because of the subdued"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "relationship between display and"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "text."}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "Books tend to go from"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "typographic contrast"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "because they're about long"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "reading, and of grabbing your"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "attention all the time."}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "On the other hand, a news layout"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "may be more this."}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "Here we're using san serif for"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "both display and textiles, but"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "their structuring weights are so"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "different that we still maintain"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "clear and strong typographic"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "contrast."}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "The display style grabbed your"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "attention, provides context,"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "this is what you're about to"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "read, and makes the layout look"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "appealing and then the textile"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "will let you read the content"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "with ease and without"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "disruption."}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "So, as you've now seen, there's"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "obviously a lot you can do in"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "terms of style pairing."}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "And I've only given you a"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "glimpse of the possibilities of"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "course."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "The key element is typographic"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "contrast."}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "Whether I did it through size,"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "weight, or style."}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "Finally, if you want to become"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "better at picking fonts, there"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "is really no way around learning"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "more about typographic styles,"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "their histories, and evolving"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "trends."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "This is how you'll become more"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "confident in front of that font"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "menu."}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "And don't worry, you won't"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "become typographic rock stars"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "overnight."}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "And yes, that's a thing."}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "But at least you know where to"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "start."}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "And I have no doubt that you'll"}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "soon grow into tremendous"}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "typographers yourself."}]}
